---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
  siteConfig,
  homeUrl,
  siteHost,
  renderTemplate,
  legalUpdatedLabel,
} from '../lib/site';

const { appName, contactDisplay: contact } = siteConfig;

const sections = [
  { id: 'acceptance', label: 'Acceptance' },
  { id: 'the-site', label: 'What this site is' },
  { id: 'download', label: 'Download and licence' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'third-party', label: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'no-warranty', label: 'No warranty' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title={siteConfig.pages.terms.title}
  description={renderTemplate(siteConfig.pages.terms.description)}
  heading="Terms of Use"
  lede="The rules for using this page and the download it provides."
  updated={legalUpdatedLabel}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    By using {siteHost}, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, stop using the site. If
    you use the site on behalf of an organisation, you confirm that you have authority to accept
    these terms for it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-site">What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    This site is operated by the publisher of the {appName} Android app. It provides the APK
    download, file details, permission list and installation notes. It is not a broadcaster, a
    league or a streaming service.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is free to read. No account or subscription is required to use it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="download">Download and licence</h2>
  <p>
    The APK is published by us and served by an external download host. That host is a separate
    service with its own terms, and this site cannot guarantee that a release will remain available,
    unchanged or compatible with your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    Any licence to use the app comes from the terms shipped with the app. Nothing on this page
    grants you a licence to the app’s content or to any broadcast.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use this site to break any law or to infringe the rights of another person;</li>
    <li>use the app to access content you are not entitled to watch;</li>
    <li>attempt to disrupt, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site or its infrastructure;</li>
    <li>scrape the site at a volume that interferes with normal use;</li>
    <li>misrepresent this site as an authorised source for any league, team, broadcaster or stream.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You are responsible for checking that installing an Android APK is permitted on your device and
    in your region, and for complying with the terms of any service you access through the app.
  </p>

  <h2 id="third-party">Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to an external download host and uses Histats for analytics, and analytics only
    starts if you allow it. Those services are separate third parties with their own terms and
    privacy policies. This site does not control their availability, content or data practices.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-warranty">No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided “as is” and “as available”. To the extent permitted by law, no warranty is
    made about accuracy, completeness, uninterrupted availability, fitness for a particular purpose,
    or the safety of any file offered by an external host. File details are checked in good faith but
    can change when a new build is published.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, this site and its operator are not liable for indirect or
    consequential loss, loss of data, device problems, service interruption, or losses arising from
    your use of the app or of a linked third-party service. Nothing in these terms limits liability
    that cannot lawfully be limited, or affects mandatory consumer rights you may have.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated as the site changes. The revision date at the top of the page shows
    the current version. Continued use after a change means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for the published site details. The address shown
    there is <a href={homeUrl}>{contact}</a>; selecting it returns to the homepage. Rights notices
    go through the <a href="/dmca/">DMCA and takedown page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
